{
  "statement": "Safety and reliability are paramount for the ATM system. SAF-01 prevents negative balances, ensuring user trust and financial safety. SAF-02 and SAF-03 provide mechanisms for secure financial transactions, safeguarding users from overdrafts. SAF-04 ensures transaction logging for accountability, while SAF-05 secures user access with PIN verification, enhancing overall safety. SAF-06 allows for safe degradation during maintenance, and SAF-07 ensures users are informed about their account status post-transaction, which fosters reliability and user confidence.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-04", "TRU-04", "RES-03"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "Requirements EFF-04, TRU-04, and RES-03 conflict with SAF-01, as they prohibit negative balances, potentially leading to delayed transactions, which undermines user safety by increasing the risk of user frustration."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-05"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "SAF-02's automatic withdrawal from savings could create resource contention with EFF-05, which aims for immediate fund withdrawals, presenting a risk to reliability during peak transaction loads."
    }
  ],
